# 2️⃣ Application Code (Intentional PMD Smell)

📄 `src/main/java/com/example/demo/Calculator.java`

This class is **intentionally written to trigger PMD warnings** (unused variable, poor practice).

```java
package com.example.demo;

public class Calculator {

    public int add(int a, int b) {
        int unused = 10;   // PMD: UnusedLocalVariable
        return a + b;
    }

    public int divide(int a, int b) {
        if (b == 0) {
            return 0;      // PMD: Avoid returning magic values
        }
        return a / b;
    }
}
```

✅ Ensures:

* Build passes
* PMD finds violations
* Pipeline fails at Code Review stage (as expected)

